---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro'
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro'
import { SITE_PRODUCT } from '../lib/site'

// Analytics is a build-time opt-in: no script tag is emitted unless both
// variables are set at build time. See src/lib/analytics.ts.
const analytics =
  import.meta.env.PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_SRC && import.meta.env.PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_DOMAIN
    ? { src: import.meta.env.PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_SRC, domain: import.meta.env.PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_DOMAIN }
    : null
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy — ${SITE_PRODUCT}`}
  description={`What the ${SITE_PRODUCT} website and desktop app store on your machine, what leaves it, and under which conditions.`}
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main-content" class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A plain inventory of what this website and the {SITE_PRODUCT} desktop app store, where the
        data lives, and what leaves your machine. Everything below is checked against the source
        code.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="website">
      <p class="mono" id="website">01 · This website</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The site stores one thing in your browser: your light or dark theme preference, kept in
          <code>localStorage</code> under the key <code>vyotiq-theme</code>. It is first-party, it
          never leaves your browser, and no cookies are set for it.
        </p>
        {analytics ? (
          <p>
            The site also runs basic, cookieless analytics. Requests carry no cookies and record no
            identifiers; we use them to count page views, nothing more.
          </p>
        ) : (
          <p>
            The site currently runs no analytics and sets no cookies. If that ever changes, this
            page will say so.
          </p>
        )}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="app-data">
      <p class="mono" id="app-data">02 · App data on your machine</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          {SITE_PRODUCT} is a desktop app. Its data lives in your per-user application data folder
          (<code>%APPDATA%\vyotiq</code> on Windows, the equivalent folder on macOS and Linux).
          Settings are stored there as <code>settings.json</code>, and each workspace keeps its
          session record under <code>workspaces/&lt;id&gt;/sessions/&lt;run&gt;/</code>:
          <code>messages.jsonl</code> for the conversation transcript and <code>events.jsonl</code>
          for telemetry event records. Both are ordinary files on your disk.
        </p>
        <p>
          Browser screenshots and downloaded files the app collects are also kept under that
          application data folder, not inside your repository.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="workspace">
      <p class="mono" id="workspace">03 · Inside the workspace</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Some agent state is written next to your code: long-term memory notes live in
          <code>.vyotiq/memory/</code> inside the repository you open, and derived search indexes in
          <code>.vyotiq/</code>. These folders belong to your project tree, so how you commit, share,
          or delete them is up to you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="outbound">
      <p class="mono" id="outbound">04 · What leaves your machine</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          <strong>Model requests.</strong> When you run a task, the prompt and the repository
          context it needs are sent to the model provider endpoint you have configured. {SITE_PRODUCT}
          does not route these requests through its own servers.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Crash and error reports.</strong> The app can send error reports to Sentry, but
          only when two conditions hold at once: the build includes a Sentry DSN, and telemetry is
          switched on in the app settings. Reports are error events, not chat transcripts. Personal
          data is explicitly excluded (<code>sendDefaultPii: false</code>), and every event is
          scrubbed by a filter before it is sent. If either condition is missing, nothing is
          initialized and nothing is sent.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Update checks.</strong> The app checks for new versions on the project's GitHub
          Releases repository (<code>vyotiqai/vyotiq-agent-v-releases</code>). Automatic download is
          disabled: the app tells you a release exists and does nothing until you choose to get it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="credentials">
      <p class="mono" id="credentials">05 · Credentials</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          API keys and tokens are kept out of <code>settings.json</code> and stored in the system
          credential storage instead. They are not written into plain settings files.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="questions">
      <p class="mono" id="questions">06 · Questions</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          For questions about this page, write to <a class="text-link" href="mailto:support@vyotiq.com">support@vyotiq.com</a>.
          The documentation covers the details in more depth:
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/concepts/privacy-data">how Agent V handles your data</a> and
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/concepts/security">the security model</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-head {
    padding: var(--space-9, 96px) 0 var(--space-6, 32px);
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: var(--space-4, 16px) 0 var(--space-5, 24px);
  }

  .lede {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .block {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-faint);
    padding: var(--space-6, 32px) 0;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .mono {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4, 16px);
  }

  .prose p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4, 16px);
  }

  .prose p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .prose code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.875em;
    background: var(--well);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-faint);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.125em 0.375em;
  }
</style>
